  "result": "Default arg `items=[]` evaluated once, at `def` time. Same list object reused every call. `append` mutates it, so state persists.\n\n```python\nadd(1)  # items is the shared default list -> [1]\nadd(2)  # same list, now [1, 2]\n```\n\nFix: use `None` sentinel, make new list per call.\n\n```python\ndef add(x, items=None):\n    if items is None:\n        items = []\n    items.append(x)\n    return items\n```\n\nNow `add(1)` -> `[1]`, `add(2)` -> `[2]`.\n\nRule: never use mutable (`[]`, `{}`, `set()`) as default. Use `None`.",
